        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: шашки",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "шашки (sháshki) — \"draughts, checkers\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "По вечерам дед играет с соседом в шашки. Po vecherám ded igráyet s sosédom v sháshki. In the evenings Grandad plays draughts with the neighbour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural. Играть в шашки (sháshki) — to play draughts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "EtymDB lists шашки (sháshki) without a source; it is usually traced to шах 'check', from Persian shāh 'king', like шахматы 'chess'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
