              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кубик (kúbik) — \"a die; a small cube\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Он бросил кубик, и выпала шестёрка. On brósil kúbik, i výpala shestyórka. He threw the die and got a six."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. A diminutive of куб — a cube. Кубики are also a child's building blocks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кубик (kúbik) is a diminutive of куб 'cube', which EtymDB traces through German Kubus and Latin cubus to Greek kýbos 'a cube'; EtymDB has no entry for кубик (kúbik)."
            }
          ]
        },
